{"id": "EUVD-2026-80635", "enisaUuid": "ba2336f6-aab3-396d-aa06-ed4e1e159e91", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: disable cc_debounce_dwork on stop\n\ncc_debounce_dwork is queued from the set_cc() and start_toggling()\ncallbacks, which run from TCPM's kthread worker.  port_stop() returns\nbefore tcpm_unregister_port() destroys that worker.  Flushing the worker\nduring unregister may therefore run a callback which queues the delayed\nwork after port_stop() has returned.\n\nThe delayed work can then run after devres has freed pmic_typec_port.\n\nUse disable_delayed_work_sync() in port_stop() to cancel a pending\ninstance and prevent the TCPM callbacks from queueing another one.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:56:43", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4359b5f95c93a4658e08368fa6fab9d89eb98447", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c614d7c44ca7fb78867ba46b233acdb59287e8c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ab669c2b44e1040ddfab7cd7f717aad580d17aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/263f7d61a4201cde16849b2d016251806e7418be"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fm22-hcrq-m39w", "CVE-2026-90027"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "040f521c-90ab-3c87-b11f-68f4caea669c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a4422ff221429c600c3dc5d0394fb3738b89d040 <1ab669c2b44e1040ddfab7cd7f717aad580d17aa"}, {"id": "17d39ac8-caf8-3d20-b415-f019bc7b155d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "30a6b6a9-4454-3b9f-a407-6381cae742c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a4422ff221429c600c3dc5d0394fb3738b89d040 <263f7d61a4201cde16849b2d016251806e7418be"}, {"id": "39bd649f-ed3f-3d07-9497-4186ba437a7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a4422ff221429c600c3dc5d0394fb3738b89d040 <4359b5f95c93a4658e08368fa6fab9d89eb98447"}, {"id": "544ee3e7-0ef1-36c0-84f8-3d8819cf3faa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5bce912e-1dbe-3054-8a45-ae871d9d2092", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "6c6052a0-9751-3c81-9336-64c667ac9a5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "b0eb31c8-8881-353c-91d6-8dbcb4888521", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a4422ff221429c600c3dc5d0394fb3738b89d040 <c614d7c44ca7fb78867ba46b233acdb59287e8c8"}, {"id": "c9e66a24-fee2-36b5-89e1-62f1dd6e470f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f0b936ef-67a8-36ae-bade-393d4ef27d4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5903ec01-2ecc-3bff-a435-b4a450560b82", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}